# Check every text file out with LF, on every OS.
#
# The validators read these files byte for byte: check 12 hashes vendored files against
# skills-lock.json, and the fault-injection suites match the constitution's tables with
# `\n`-anchored patterns. A Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true rewrites them to CRLF,
# so the lock reports untouched upstream files as "modified locally" and the rule-ownership
# cases cannot find the table they edit — red locally while CI on Linux is green.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip binary
